{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/861775-lo8md-exorcise-elemental-spirit-in-crossover","id":861775,"title":"[Lo8MD]Exorcise Elemental Spirit in crossover.","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-04-08T06:14:32-07:00","id":861775,"title":"[Lo8MD]Exorcise Elemental Spirit in crossover.","content":"Hello.<br /> <br /> One of my players plays a hsien (Land of Eight Millon Dreams sourcebook to CtD2) in my crossover chronicle. She wants to use his Alchemy to Exorcise Elemental Spirit in order to get rid of a bunch of banes and fomores. And I am confused - do banes count spirits in the Alchemy's point of view? The hsien's magic is very strongly element-oriented, and even if a hsien is able to exorcise wyrm spirits, what Element the hsien should use?<br /> <br /> Sure I am aware of the &quot;Storyteller can treat how he likes&quot; and the other stuff, but maybe anybody have had similar issues? Any suggestions but the obvious ones are welcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-08T14:58:29-07:00","id":862203,"title":"","content":"That should be possible. However, banes are not pre-categorized to make things easy for it, and to top that off, a lot of the more accessible stuff uses a newer system than the one presented in Lo8MD, using Essence in place of Power and changing how a number of Charms work. What's more, even if you manage to exorcise a bane from a fomor, you'd better be ready to heal the possessed unfortunate on the spot, or they will die of ten unsoakable levels of aggravated damage, applied one per turn. If you are using Essence instead of Power, the sum typically adds up to the total of a spirit's Rage, Gnosis, and Willpower, so adjust spirit-based powers accordingly; very powerful banes like nexus crawlers or dream makers, however, can have a good deal more, and don't get the same reduction.<br /> <br /> As to how to get a hold on which element a bane falls under, consult the description of elemental souls. Just about any bane of malign psychology or emotions can probably be placed under the auspices of one of the wu xing based on what kind of bad vibe they feed off of. Some elemental banes might convert readily, but the hoglings might cause problems, because they're banes of air. If necessary to know, just give it the Yin and Yang ratings associated with elementals of said element. Some might get weird, though, such as the aforementioned nexus crawler; where it fits is not so clear. Ditto for dream makers, which are primordial fashioners of the universe gone bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-11T00:51:37-07:00","id":863520,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/861775-lo8md-exorcise-elemental-spirit-in-crossover?p=862203#post862203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As to how to get a hold on which element a bane falls under, consult the description of elemental souls. Just about any bane of malign psychology or emotions can probably be placed under the auspices of one of the wu xing based on what kind of bad vibe they feed off of.</div> </div> </div> </div>This suggestion is very helpful! Thank you.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11161-leeder","name":"Leeder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11161_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"25"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}